(ns verify-protocol-lib-substance
  "A repo can be named after a wire protocol and never touch a byte.

  `orgs/kotoba-lang/com-modbus-tcp` says, in its own README, that it is a
  \"clean-room API-compatible implementation of the modbus_tcp deep system
  protocol\". Its entire source is 182 lines of `(def entity-specs [...])` +
  `(def routes ...)` producing `POST /v1/requests`, `GET /v1/responses/{id}`,
  and so on -- a generic CRUD-over-HTTP facade. It contains zero bitwise or
  byte operations. It does not implement Modbus. Sitting one directory over,
  `orgs/kotoba-lang/org-modbus` is 558 lines across pdu.cljc/crc.cljc/
  rtu.cljc/tcp.cljc with 77 bitwise/byte operations -- a real wire codec for
  the same protocol.

  Nothing in this workspace's existing indices can tell these two repos
  apart: same naming convention, same west manifest shape, same concept
  index, and the maturity scorer (`scripts/repo-maturity.cljk`) scores on
  total bytes + scaffold-marker hits, so `com-modbus-tcp` comes back CLEAN
  (`scaffold-marker-hits 0`) -- the instrument that is supposed to catch
  scaffolding cannot see this particular scaffold, because it doesn't look
  like a TODO or a stub, it looks like a complete, if generic, actor.

  This is not one mistake. `orgs/kotoba-lang/` carries roughly a thousand
  `com-*` repos generated from the same template (`src/<name>/main.cljc`,
  `entity-specs` + `routes` + `/v1/*`), and the audit that produced this
  script found the template's entity vocabulary was itself copy-pasted
  across unrelated domains: `com-nmea2000-marine` (a marine CAN protocol)
  carries the entity list `Vehicle, Signal, ChargeSession, Connector, Trip,
  Command` -- an EV-charging (OCPP) schema -- and 47 payment-rail repos
  (`com-fedwire`, `com-zengin-system`, `com-sepa-ct`, `com-chips-clearing`,
  `com-ach-network`, ...) all share Stripe's own object model verbatim:
  `Charge, Customer, PaymentIntent, PaymentMethod, Payout, Refund`.

  ## The rule

  A repo is a CANDIDATE (`rest-facade`) when some file under its `src/` tree
  defines `entity-specs`, defines `routes`, and mentions a `/v1/` path --
  the fingerprint of this specific generator, found by scanning content, not
  by matching a filename (`main.cljc` is what the generator happens to call
  it; a repo that used a different filename for the same shape should not
  slip past on a technicality).

  A candidate CLAIMS to be a protocol/format/codec library when its own
  README (or, failing that, its own top-of-file docstring) says so, in its
  own words, within the first ~1000 characters: `protocol`, `codec`, `wire
  format`, `binary format`. This is not a domain-vocabulary guess by this
  script -- it is what the repo's own generated description already
  declares itself to be (\"...implementation of the modbus_tcp deep system
  protocol...\" / \"...fedwire legacy/deep financial protocol...\"), lifted
  verbatim. A REST wrapper around Stripe's own API legitimately says
  \"platform\", not \"protocol\", and is deliberately not in this set --
  see the false-positive-control note below.

  A claiming candidate is a FINDING when the byte/bit-operation count across
  its whole `src/` tree (not just the facade file -- a repo could
  legitimately keep wire logic in a sibling file while `main.cljc` is a thin
  REST shell over it) is zero (`protocol-facade-no-wire-code`, error) or
  merely 1-2 (`protocol-facade-thin-wire-code`, warn -- present for
  completeness; measured 2026-08-29 on a 1-in-5 sample of
  `orgs/kotoba-lang/com-*`, this bucket was empty: the generator produces
  either a pure facade or nothing in this shape, not a thin middle).

  Supporting, not decisive, evidence attached to each finding: how many
  OTHER scanned repos share this repo's exact entity-name signature. High
  sharing is evidence of template generation independent of domain; the
  `com-modbus-tcp` case shows sharing is not required for the finding to be
  correct -- its own entity names (`MbapHeader`, `Request`, `Response`,
  `ExceptionResponse`) are Modbus-flavoured and mostly unshared, and it is
  still a finding, because the decisive signal is the zero byte operations,
  not the entity names.

  ## What this deliberately does NOT flag, and why

  A repo with the `entity-specs`/`routes`/`/v1/` shape that does NOT claim
  protocol/codec/format in its own words is not flagged. A REST API client
  for a genuine REST platform (payment gateway dashboards, SaaS CRUD APIs)
  legitimately has routes, entities and zero bitwise operations -- that is
  what a correct implementation of a REST platform looks like. This script
  cannot and does not try to tell 'com-somesaas is a correct REST facade'
  from 'com-somesaas is an incorrect REST facade of a REST platform that
  actually needed more logic' -- that question is out of scope. It only
  catches the narrower, machine-checkable claim: 'this repo says of ITSELF
  that it is a protocol/codec/format, and then contains no code that
  encodes or decodes anything'.

  A repo that claims protocol/codec/format but does NOT have the
  entity-specs/routes/v1 facade shape is not flagged, even with zero
  bitwise operations -- e.g. a pure spec/reference-data repo with no code at
  all is a different, legitimate defect class (missing implementation, not
  a facade masquerading as an implementation) and is out of scope here.

  ## What this cannot answer

  Entity-signature sharing counts are bounded by what is actually checked
  out on this machine (`orgs/` is a cone-mode sparse checkout of a ~4,260
  repo west manifest; most entries are not present on disk and cannot be
  read at all -- see CLAUDE.md, 'sparse cone'). A reported sharing count of
  N means 'N others among what I could read', never 'N total in the
  workspace' -- the true count is >= N, never assumed <=. Registered repos
  that are not checked out are counted as UNVERIFIED, never as clean, and
  are reported separately from repos this script actually opened and read."
  (:require ["fs" :as fs] ["path" :as p] [clojure.string :as str]))

(def argv (vec (drop 2 (.-argv js/process))))
(defn flag [n] (some #{n} argv))
(defn opt [n d] (let [i (.indexOf argv n)] (if (neg? i) d (get argv (inc i) d))))
(def root (opt "--root" "."))
(def findings? (flag "--findings"))
(def json? (flag "--json"))

(defn ls [d] (try (vec (.readdirSync fs d)) (catch :default _ ::error)))
(defn dir? [f] (try (.isDirectory (.statSync fs f)) (catch :default _ false)))
(defn slurp* [f] (try (.readFileSync fs f "utf8") (catch :default e [::error (.-message e)])))
(defn ok? [x] (not (and (vector? x) (= ::error (first x)))))

;; Directories not authored by this repo, or not source: build output,
;; caches, vendored trees, scratch.
(def skip-dir
  #"/(node_modules|\.git|\.shadow-cljs|\.cache|target|dist|build|out|coverage|vendor|_archive|_working)(/|$)")

(def src-ext #"\.(cljc|clj|cljs)$")

(defn walk [d depth acc]
  (if (or (> depth 5) (re-find skip-dir (str d "/")) (>= (count acc) 400))
    acc
    (let [entries (ls d)]
      (if (= entries ::error)
        acc
        (reduce (fn [a e]
                  (let [f (p/join d e)]
                    (cond
                      (dir? f) (walk f (inc depth) a)
                      (re-find src-ext f) (conj a f)
                      :else a)))
                acc entries)))))

;; --- signals -------------------------------------------------------------

(def entity-re #":entity\s+\"([^\"]+)\"")
(def routes-def-re #"\(def\s+routes\b")
(def bitop-re #"\b(bit-and|bit-or|bit-xor|bit-shift-left|bit-shift-right|unsigned-bit-shift-right|unchecked-byte|byte-array)\b")
(def claim-re #"(?i)(protocol|codec|wire[- ]format|binary[- ]format)")

(defn entities-in [text]
  (into (sorted-set) (map second) (re-seq entity-re text)))

(defn bitop-count [text] (count (re-seq bitop-re text)))

(defn line-count [text] (count (str/split-lines text)))

(defn claim-snippet
  "First claim-bearing sentence-ish fragment from the given text, or nil."
  [text]
  (when-let [m (re-find claim-re text)]
    (let [kw (if (string? m) m (first m))
          i (.indexOf text kw)
          start (max 0 (- i 60))
          end (min (count text) (+ i 40))]
      (-> (subs text start end) str/trim (str/replace #"\s+" " ")))))

;; --- west registry ---------------------------------------------------------

(defn west-paths []
  (let [y (slurp* (p/join root "manifest" "west.yml"))]
    (when (ok? y)
      (into #{} (map second) (re-seq #"(?m)^\s*path:\s*(\S+)\s*$" y)))))

;; --- per-repo scan -----------------------------------------------------

(defn scan-repo
  "Returns nil on unreadable repo dir, else a map describing what was found.
  Never returns a false 'clean' for something that could not be read --
  unreadability is reported by the caller as a distinct bucket."
  [rel abs]
  (let [src (p/join abs "src")]
    (if-not (dir? src)
      {:repo rel :status :not-facade-shape :reason "no src/ directory"}
      (let [files (walk src 0 [])]
        (if (empty? files)
          {:repo rel :status :not-facade-shape :reason "src/ has no .cljc/.clj/.cljs files"}
          (let [contents (keep (fn [f] (let [c (slurp* f)] (when (ok? c) [f c]))) files)
                unread (- (count files) (count contents))
                blob (str/join "\n" (map second contents))
                entities (entities-in blob)
                routes? (boolean (re-find routes-def-re blob))
                v1? (str/includes? blob "/v1/")
                facade? (and (seq entities) routes? v1?)]
            (if-not facade?
              (cond-> {:repo rel :status :not-facade-shape}
                (pos? unread) (assoc :unread-files unread))
              (let [test-dir (p/join abs "test")
                    test-files (if (dir? test-dir) (walk test-dir 0 []) [])
                    test-blob (->> test-files
                                   (keep (fn [f] (let [c (slurp* f)] (when (ok? c) c))))
                                   (str/join "\n"))
                    readme (p/join abs "README.md")
                    readme-text (let [c (slurp* readme)] (when (ok? c) c))
                    doc-text (subs blob 0 (min (count blob) 800))
                    [claim? claim-src claim-text]
                    (cond
                      (and readme-text (re-find claim-re (subs readme-text 0 (min (count readme-text) 1000))))
                      [true :readme (claim-snippet (subs readme-text 0 (min (count readme-text) 1000)))]

                      (re-find claim-re doc-text)
                      [true :docstring (claim-snippet doc-text)]

                      :else [false nil nil])]
                {:repo rel
                 :status :facade
                 :files (count contents)
                 :unread-files unread
                 :lines (reduce + (map (comp line-count second) contents))
                 :entities entities
                 :signature (str/join "," entities)
                 :bitops (bitop-count blob)
                 :test-bitops (bitop-count test-blob)
                 :claims? claim?
                 :claim-source claim-src
                 :claim-text claim-text}))))))))

;; --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

(defn -main []
  (let [registered (west-paths)
        orgs-dir (p/join root "orgs")]
    (when-not registered
      (println "REFUSED\tno manifest/west.yml under" root
                "-- cannot tell a registered checkout from a stale/unregistered one")
      (.exit js/process 2))
    (when-not (dir? orgs-dir)
      (println "REFUSED\tno orgs/ under" root "-- nothing to scan")
      (.exit js/process 2))
    (let [org-registered (into #{} (filter #(str/starts-with? % "orgs/")) registered)
          org-entries (ls orgs-dir)
          checked-out (if (= org-entries ::error)
                        []
                        (for [o org-entries :when (dir? (p/join orgs-dir o))
                              r (let [e (ls (p/join orgs-dir o))] (if (= e ::error) [] e))
                              :let [rel (str "orgs/" o "/" r)]
                              :when (and (contains? org-registered rel) (dir? (p/join root rel)))]
                          rel))
          unverified (- (count org-registered) (count checked-out))
          scan-results (mapv (fn [rel] (scan-repo rel (p/join root rel))) checked-out)
          scanned (count scan-results)]
      (when (zero? scanned)
        (println "REFUSED\tzero registered orgs/ checkouts were present on disk to scan"
                  "-- a run that examines nothing has not measured the rule")
        (.exit js/process 2))
      (let [unread-repos (filter #(and (= :not-facade-shape (:status %))
                                        (nil? (:reason %))
                                        (pos? (:unread-files % 0)))
                                  scan-results)
            not-facade (filter #(= :not-facade-shape (:status %)) scan-results)
            facade (filter #(= :facade (:status %)) scan-results)
            facade-no-claim (remove :claims? facade)
            claiming (filter :claims? facade)
            errors (filter #(zero? (:bitops %)) claiming)
            thin (filter #(<= 1 (:bitops %) 2) claiming)
            clean-claiming (filter #(> (:bitops %) 2) claiming)
            ;; entity-signature sharing, scoped to what was actually read.
            sig->repos (reduce (fn [m {:keys [repo signature]}]
                                  (if (str/blank? signature) m
                                      (update m signature (fnil conj []) repo)))
                                {} facade)
            sharing-detail (fn [{:keys [repo signature]}]
                              (let [siblings (remove #{repo} (get sig->repos signature []))]
                                {:count (count siblings) :examples (vec (take 3 siblings))}))
            finding-line (fn [severity key detail] (str "FINDING\t" severity "\t" key "\t" detail))
            findings
            (concat
              (for [{:keys [repo bitops lines files test-bitops claim-source claim-text] :as row} errors]
                (let [{:keys [count examples]} (sharing-detail row)]
                  (finding-line
                    "error" (str "protocol-facade-no-wire-code:" repo)
                    (str "claims protocol/codec/format (" (name claim-source) ": \"" claim-text "\"); "
                         "entity-specs+routes+/v1/ REST-facade shape (" files " file(s), " lines " lines); "
                         "0 bit/byte operations across the whole src/ tree"
                         (when (pos? test-bitops) (str " (tests have " test-bitops " though)"))
                         "; entity-signature \"" (:signature row) "\" shared with " count " other scanned repo(s)"
                         (when (seq examples) (str " e.g. " (str/join " " examples)))
                         "."))))
              (for [{:keys [repo bitops lines files claim-source claim-text] :as row} thin]
                (let [{:keys [count examples]} (sharing-detail row)]
                  (finding-line
                    "warn" (str "protocol-facade-thin-wire-code:" repo)
                    (str "claims protocol/codec/format (" (name claim-source) ": \"" claim-text "\"); "
                         "entity-specs+routes+/v1/ REST-facade shape (" files " file(s), " lines " lines); "
                         "only " bitops " bit/byte operation(s) across the whole src/ tree; "
                         "entity-signature shared with " count " other scanned repo(s)"
                         (when (seq examples) (str " e.g. " (str/join " " examples)))
                         "."))))
              )]
        (if json?
          (println (.stringify js/JSON
                                (clj->js {:scanned scanned
                                          :registered-under-orgs (count org-registered)
                                          :checked-out (count checked-out)
                                          :unverified-not-checked-out unverified
                                          :not-facade-shape (count not-facade)
                                          :unreadable-files (count unread-repos)
                                          :facade-total (count facade)
                                          :facade-no-protocol-claim (count facade-no-claim)
                                          :facade-claims-protocol (count claiming)
                                          :facade-claims-clean (count clean-claiming)
                                          :findings-error (count errors)
                                          :findings-warn (count thin)
                                          :error-repos (mapv :repo errors)
                                          :warn-repos (mapv :repo thin)})
                                nil 2))
          (do
            (when findings?
              (doseq [l findings] (println l)))
            (println (str "SCANNED\t" scanned
                          "\tregistered orgs/ checkouts present on disk and readable, of "
                          (count org-registered) " registered under orgs/ ("
                          unverified " not checked out -> UNVERIFIED, not scanned)"))
            (println (str "not-facade-shape=" (count not-facade)
                          " facade-no-protocol-claim=" (count facade-no-claim)
                          " facade-claims-protocol=" (count claiming)
                          " (clean=" (count clean-claiming)
                          " thin=" (count thin) " no-wire-code=" (count errors) ")"))
            (println (str "protocol-facade-no-wire-code=" (count errors)
                          " protocol-facade-thin-wire-code=" (count thin)))
            (when (pos? unverified)
              (println (str "UNVERIFIED\t" unverified
                            "\tregistered checkouts not present on disk (sparse checkout) -- "
                            "not examined, not reported clean")))))
        (.exit js/process (if (or (seq errors) (seq thin)) 1 0))))))

(-main)
